# The build tree. The compiled component is committed -- `tb-ants.wasm` and the generated manifests
# beside it are what the platform loads, and the machine that loads them has no Rust toolchain --
# but what produced them is not the artifact.
target/

# Local run artifacts.
.run/

# THE BUILD OUTPUT IS NOT COMMITTED. It is carried in the artifact image `Dockerfile` builds --
# `tinybrains/ants:dev` locally, `ghcr.io/tiny-brains/ants:<tag>` published -- and every consumer
# takes it from there rather than from a sibling checkout of this directory.
#
# WHY IT CHANGED. A committed component made "all ten repositories in one parent directory" the
# only layout the platform builds in, and it was not even reproducible: rustc bakes the absolute
# path of every source file a panic can name into the binary, so the artifact that used to live
# here carried one machine's ~/.cargo path and nobody else could rebuild it byte for byte. The
# Dockerfile pins the toolchain and remaps those paths, so the digest is a function of the SOURCE.
#
# `./build.sh` still writes all of this, and still has to be run before viz/build.sh or the host
# tools. It is just no longer the thing that ships.
tb-ants.wasm
plugin.json
cartridge.json
reference/observations.json
viz/dist/

# GENERATED by build.sh from maps/ -- the boards themselves are source and stay committed.
src/maps_gen.rs
